# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Lampose User App — environment
#
# Copy to `.env`. Expo inlines every EXPO_PUBLIC_* variable at BUILD time, so
# a change here needs the dev server restarted (and a rebuild for a release
# binary) — there is no runtime environment to read on a phone.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── The backend ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The API origin, WITHOUT a trailing slash and WITHOUT `/api`.
#
#   right   http://192.168.1.5:5001
#   right   https://api.lampose.com
#   wrong   http://192.168.1.5:5001/api      ← that is the web frontend's form
#
# Every path in services/api/endpoints.ts already starts `/api/v2/...`, the
# same way Backend/routes/index.js writes them, so a route can be read off one
# file and found in the other. A trailing `/api` is stripped defensively, but
# do not rely on it.
#
# LEAVE IT UNSET IN DEVELOPMENT and the app derives the host from wherever
# Metro served the bundle, on port 5001 — which is the machine running the
# backend in every setup in this repo. That is what makes a physical phone
# work without editing this file on every network change. The Android
# emulator is special-cased to 10.0.2.2. See services/api/config.ts.
#
# SET IT for anything else: a release build, a device on a different network
# from the dev machine, or a staging backend.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://192.168.1.5:5001

# `extra.apiUrl` in app.json is read as a fallback, for the case where a build
# pipeline can write app config but not environment variables.


# ── Which API version ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Not configurable, and deliberately so.
#
# This app is a v2 client on every route — the same public surface lampose.com
# reads. v1 is the onboarding and admin surface: its writes create properties
# on a Lampose employee's behalf and need an administrator's grant, and a
# student's phone has no business reaching it. The version is written into
# each path in endpoints.ts rather than being a setting, so it cannot be
# repointed by an environment variable.
